    "background_story": "Theo was once a devout Catholic, but after a series of tragic events, he became disillusioned with the church and began to seek answers in the darker corners of spirituality. He delved deep into the occult, eventually finding solace in the teachings of Satanism. Theo saw the devil as a symbol of rebellion against the oppressive forces that had wronged him. As he immersed himself in the Satanic community, he adopted the moniker 'The Apostate' and quickly gained notoriety for his charismatic sermons and unapologetic views. Theo's message of self-empowerment and individualism resonated with many, but also drew the ire of those who saw him as a servant of darkness. Despite the controversy, Theo remained unapologetic, convinced that his path was the only one that could bring him true freedom and power.",
